===Goal-line technology===
For the second year in a row, [[goal-line technology]] was used for the tournament.<ref name="draw">{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=2193035/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131009190722/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=2193035/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=9 October 2013|title=Morocco awaits continental champions, confirms goal-line technology|publisher=FIFA.com|date=9 October 2013}}</ref> GoalControl GmbH was chosen as the official goal-line technology provider.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/aboutfifa/organisation/marketing/qualityprogramme/news/newsid=2193485/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131010172618/http://www.fifa.com/aboutfifa/organisation/marketing/qualityprogramme/news/newsid=2193485/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=10 October 2013|title=GoalControl confirmed as goal-line technology provider for Brazil 2014|publisher=FIFA.com|date=10 October 2013}}</ref>

===Vanishing spray===
Following successful trials at the [[2013 FIFA U-20 World Cup]] and [[2013 FIFA U-17 World Cup]], FIFA approved the [[vanishing spray]] to be used by the tournament referees to mark the ten-yard line for the defending team during a free kick.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/aboutfifa/footballdevelopment/technicalsupport/refereeing/news/newsid=2226962/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131122063300/http://www.fifa.com/aboutfifa/footballdevelopment/technicalsupport/refereeing/news/newsid=2226962/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=22 November 2013|title=Largely positive experience with the use of vanishing spray in FIFA competitions|publisher=FIFA.com|date=20 November 2013}}</ref>

==Squads==
{{main|2013 FIFA Club World Cup squads}}

Each team named a 23-man squad (three of whom must be goalkeepers) by the FIFA deadline of 29 November 2013. Injury replacements were allowed until 24 hours before the team's first match.<ref name="regulations"/>

A total of 31 nationalities were represented in the squads of the seven teams.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=2239340/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131205115308/http://www.fifa.com//clubworldcup/news/newsid=2239340/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=5 December 2013|title=Cosmopolitan cast list promises much|publisher=FIFA.com|date=5 December 2013}}</ref>

==Matches==
[[File:QF Play off, 2013 FIFA CWC.jpg|thumb|Quarter final playoff in Agadir]]
The draw was held on 9 October 2013 at 19:00 [[Western European Summer Time|WEST]] ([[UTC+01:00|UTC+1]]), at the La Mamounia Hotel in [[Marrakesh]], to decide the "positions" in the bracket for the three teams which entered the quarter-finals (champions of AFC, CAF, and CONCACAF).<ref name="draw"/><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=2192800/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131011235521/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=2192800/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=11 October 2013|title=Relive the Morocco 2013 draw|publisher=FIFA.com|date=9 October 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=2192706/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131012030109/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=2192706/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=12 October 2013|title=Draw paves the way in Marrakech|publisher=FIFA.com|date=9 October 2013}}</ref>

If a match was tied after normal playing time:<ref name="regulations"/>
*For elimination matches, [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]] was played. If still tied after extra time, a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]] was held to determine the winner.
*For the matches for fifth place and third place, no extra time was played, and a penalty shoot-out was held to determine the winner.
